This adaptation is dedicated to the people who studied, preserved, and translated EarthBound, making it possible to rediscover it on modern computers.

Thank you to Nintendo, Shigesato Itoi, APE, HAL Laboratory, and the original teams for creating this work. Thank you to the players and communities for their love, research, documentation, tools, and translations.
Projects and Contributors
- Native C codebase: Brian Pugh and contributors to BrianPugh/earthbound.
  https://github.com/BrianPugh/earthbound
  Revision used: a2cf5c327d367d90440c5768713056462b0c4d9e.
- SPC700/DSP audio: LakeSnes authors and contributors.
- Windowing, video, audio, and controllers: Sam Lantinga and SDL2 contributors.
- tamp compression: Brian Pugh and contributors, under the included license.
- Data embedding in private builds: Dale Weiler/incbin.
- Campaign checkpoints: FantasyAnime’s public save collection and its contributors.
  https://fantasyanime.com/legacy/earthb_saves.htm
- Linux/macOS SDL2 libraries: Sourced from TheRunaway5’s Phase Distorter 0.5 packages. That project’s game executable was not reused.
- Build tools: Zig/Clang, Python, CMake, Ninja, and ebtools.
- Desktop adaptation, menus, and adjustments: Edzito, with assistance from Codex.
